Delta Air Lines (NYSE: DAL) guides on the following financial metrics in its quarterly earnings outlooks (as of April 7, 2025):

1. Total revenue growth (year over year, %): For the March 2025 quarter, Delta expected revenue growth of 7% to 9%, per its January 2025 call.
2. Operating margin (%): Delta expected to expand margins by about 2 points in the March 2025 quarter.
3. Earnings per share (adjusted EPS): Delta expected first-quarter 2025 adjusted EPS of $0.70 to $1.00; full-year 2025 EPS was guided to greater than $7.35.
4. Capacity growth (ASMs, year over year %): Full-year 2025 capacity growth of 3% to 4%.
5. Unit cost excluding fuel (CASM-ex, year over year %): Full-year 2025 CASM-ex growth expected to be low single digits.
6. Fuel price per gallon: The company's guidance deck includes a fuel price assumption for each quarter (confirmed for the 2024 deck; not confirmed for the March 2025 quarter).
7. Free cash flow and leverage (full-year): Delta's guidance deck has included free cash flow and adjusted debt to EBITDAR targets (confirmed for the 2024 deck).

Caveats: Items 1 to 5 are confirmed by specific January 2025 statements. Items 6 and 7 come from the 2024 guidance deck and may not match the March 2025 quarter outlook exactly. Search results dated after April 7, 2025 were excluded. Delta's guidance is generally on an adjusted (non-GAAP) basis.

